@startuml Perceptor data
' Perceptor data: the plugin declares a struct, the core keeps the storage.
' SQLite: a file per perceptor; Postgres: a schema per perceptor.

participant "Perceptor\n(plugin)" as P
participant "perceplib\nStore[T]" as S
participant "Core\n(plugin manager)" as Core
participant "Import chain\n(closer)" as Chain
database "Main DB\n(items)" as DB
database "Perceptor\nstorage" as PDB

== Registration ==
Core -> P: Schema()
P -> S: Places.Schema()
S --> Core: name, version, fields\n(from T by reflection)
Core -> PDB: create / migrate\n(sqlite: perceptors/geo.db,\npostgres: schema perceptor_geo)
note right of Core: a new schema version:\nrebuild, queue the items again

== Import (Single) ==
Chain -> P: Decorate(item)
P -> S: Places.Put(item, Location{...})
S -> S: the value rides on the item
Chain -> DB: item
Chain -> PDB: the perceptor's values\n(guid, version, pass)

== Order ==
Core -> PDB: values for the shown guids
Core -> P: Order(anchor, items)
P -> S: Places.Get(item)
S --> P: Location, ok
P --> Core: entries (guid, section?)

== Deletion ==
Core -> DB: item deleted
Core -> PDB: delete its rows\n(every perceptor)

== Later: Group ==
note over P, PDB: a pass over the library (or what changed), not the import chain:\nGroup(items) -> Trips.Put(Trip{...}, guids) -> groups + "photo -> group"\nin the perceptor's storage; Order gives the sheet by groups (sections)
@enduml
